@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Plan
+
+## Constraints
+- Tests first: write each task's test, see it fail, then implement.
+- Every task leaves the code and the existing tests passing.
+- Respect layering (domain does not import application); use the existing `new_id` helper.
+- Persistence failure behaviour and non-chat events are unchanged.
+
+## Task 1: build_turn_messages takes ids
+- Files: `backend/src/pharma_agent/domain/conversation/turns.py`; update callers (`application/chat/service.py`
+  temporarily passes `new_id()`) and existing test callers; test in `backend/tests/domain/test_conversation.py`.
+- Interfaces: provides required kwargs `user_message_id`, `assistant_message_id`.
+- Test: messages carry exactly the given ids.
+
+## Task 2: session ids, events, result
+- Files: `application/chat/service.py`; tests in `backend/tests/application/test_chat_service.py`.
+- Uses: Task 1. Provides: `ChatSession.user_message_id/assistant_message_id`, `message_id` on the
+  first event, `persisted`/`created_at` on `done`, new `ChatTurnResult` fields.
+- Test: ids distinct, read-only, match first event, stored messages, done and result; created_at equals stored time.
+
+## Task 3: remove error event
+- Files: `application/progress.py`, `domain/agent/run.py`, `application/chat/service.py`, `README.md`;
+  test in `test_chat_service.py` (replaces the persist-failure test).
+- Test: failed save ends with `done` (persisted false, message_id None), no error event, answer delivered.
+
+## Task 4: CLI message
+- Files: `backend/src/pharma_agent/cli.py`, `backend/tests/test_cli.py`.
+- Uses: `persisted` on `done` (Task 2). Remove ERROR branch (Task 3).
+- Test: `_render` of done with persisted false writes the message to stderr; true prints nothing.
+
+## Final
+Run `uv run pytest` in `backend/` and fix failures.
